%U A402147 2,6,1,4,1,2,3,3,2,6,1,5,1,2,1,12,2,2,2
%N A402147 Number of 1-based non-restricted growth permutations of the prime indices of n.
%C A402147 A 1-based restricted growth sequence of length j is a sequence (a_1, ..., a_j), satisfying a_1 = 1 and a_i <= 1 + max(a_1, ..., a_{i-1}) for all i = 2, 3, ..., j. We also include the empty sequence.
%C A402147 A prime index of n is a number m such that prime(m) divides n. The multiset of prime indices of n is row n of A112798, sum A056239.
%e A402147 The non-1-based restricted growth sequences of {1,1,2,3} are: (1132), (1312), (1321), (2113), (2131), (2311), (3112), (3121), (3211), so a(60) = 9. Missing are: (1123), (1213), (1231).
%e A402147 The a(n) permutations for n = 3, 10, 20, 30, 40, 42, 60, 84:
%e A402147   (2)  (13)  (113)  (132)  (1113)  (124)  (1132)  (1124)
%e A402147        (31)  (131)  (213)  (1131)  (142)  (1312)  (1142)
%e A402147              (311)  (231)  (1311)  (214)  (1321)  (1214)
%e A402147                     (312)  (3111)  (241)  (2113)  (1241)
%e A402147                     (321)          (412)  (2131)  (1412)
%e A402147                                    (421)  (2311)  (1421)
%e A402147                                           (3112)  (2114)
%e A402147                                           (3121)  (2141)
%e A402147                                           (3211)  (2411)
%e A402147                                                   (4112)
%e A402147                                                   (4121)
%e A402147                                                   (4211)
%t A402147 prix[n_]:=If[n==1,{},Flatten[Cases[FactorInteger[n],{p_,k_}:>Table[PrimePi[p],{k}]]]];
%t A402147 rgoQ[y_]:=y=={}||y[[1]]==1&&And@@Table[y[[i]]<=1+Max@@Take[y,i-1],{i,2,Length[y]}];
%t A402147 Table[Length[Select[Permutations[prix[n]],Not@*rgoQ]],{n,100}]
%Y A402147 Positions of 1 starting at n = 2 are counted by A000005.
%Y A402147 Positions of 0 are A000079, counted by all ones.
%Y A402147 Allowing restricted growth gives A008480, firsts A358526.
%Y A402147 Positions of positive terms are A057716, counted by A000065.
%Y A402147 The complement is counted by A402146, firsts A402152.
%Y A402147 For a multiset with prescribed multiplicities we have A402149, complement A402150.
%Y A402147 Positions of first appearances are A402151, firsts in A402147.
%Y A402147 A011782 counts compositions, strict A032020.
%Y A402147 A055932 ranks normal partitions, counted by A047967.
%Y A402147 A080259 ranks non-normal partitions, counted by A000065.
%Y A402147 A383253 counts restricted growth compositions, triangle A383713, ranks A402139.
%Y A402147 A402138 counts non-restricted growth compositions, triangle A402142, ranks A402141.
